  T "MLA.GEO.SIM.3" "Two triangles have side ratios 2, 2, and 3. Is SSS similarity justified?" "No, all three side ratios must be equal." "SSS similarity requires the same ratio for every corresponding side pair." "Yes, two ratios match." "All three ratios must match, not only two." "Yes, any ratio greater than 1 works." "The actual ratio value matters less than equality across all pairs." "No, side ratios are never used." "SSS similarity is based on side ratios.",
  T "MLA.GEO.SIM.3" "Which evidence is enough for AA similarity?" "Two pairs of corresponding angles are congruent." "Two angle pairs establish triangle similarity because the third angle pair must also match." "One pair of sides is congruent." "One side pair alone does not establish similarity." "One side ratio is known." "One ratio alone is insufficient." "The triangles are drawn with the same orientation." "Orientation is not a similarity criterion.",
