  T "MLA.GEO.SIM.3" "A dilation maps one triangle to a triangle congruent to another. What conclusion is supported?" "The original triangle is similar to the other triangle." "Dilation supports similarity, and congruence-preserving motion can complete the mapping." "The triangles have no relationship." "The transformation sequence gives a relationship." "The original triangle must be larger." "Dilation may enlarge or reduce depending on scale factor." "Only one angle is related." "A dilation preserves all angle measures.",
  T "MLA.GEO.SIM.3" "Two triangles have sides 6, 8, 10 and 9, 12, 15. Which statement is true?" "They are similar by SSS similarity." "Each side in the second triangle is 1.5 times the corresponding side in the first." "They are congruent by SSS." "The side lengths are not equal, so congruence is not shown." "They cannot be similar because sizes differ." "Similar triangles may have different sizes." "They are similar by AA only." "The given evidence is side ratios, not angle pairs.",
  T "MLA.GEO.SIM.3" "A pair of triangles has one congruent angle but no side information. What can be concluded?" "Similarity is not justified yet." "One angle pair alone is not enough for a triangle similarity criterion." "AA similarity applies." "AA needs two angle pairs." "SSS similarity applies." "SSS needs three side ratios." "SAS similarity applies." "SAS needs two side ratios and the included angle.",
  T "MLA.GEO.SIM.3" "In SAS similarity, which angle must be congruent?" "The included angle between the proportional sides" "SAS similarity uses the angle included by the two proportional side pairs." "Any angle in either triangle" "The angle must be between the proportional sides." "The largest angle only" "The criterion depends on included position, not size." "The right angle only" "SAS similarity applies beyond right triangles.",
  T "MLA.GEO.SIM.3" "Triangles have side ratios <sup>4</sup>&frasl;<sub>8</sub>, <sup>5</sup>&frasl;<sub>10</sub>, and <sup>6</sup>&frasl;<sub>12</sub>. What criterion is supported?" "SSS similarity" "All three ratios equal &frac12;, so SSS similarity is supported." "AA similarity" "No angle pairs are provided." "SAS similarity" "The evidence gives all three sides, not an included angle." "No similarity" "The ratios are equal, so similarity is supported.",
