  T "MLA.GEO.TRI.4" "Which ratio does not use the hypotenuse?" "Tangent" "Tangent uses opposite over adjacent." "Sine" "Sine uses the hypotenuse." "Cosine" "Cosine uses the hypotenuse." "Both sine and cosine" "Both sine and cosine include the hypotenuse.",
  T "MLA.GEO.TRI.4" "SOH means which ratio?" "sin = <sup>opposite</sup>&frasl;<sub>hypotenuse</sub>" "SOH stands for sine, opposite, hypotenuse." "cos = <sup>opposite</sup>&frasl;<sub>hypotenuse</sub>" "Cosine is represented by CAH." "tan = <sup>opposite</sup>&frasl;<sub>hypotenuse</sub>" "Tangent is represented by TOA." "sin = <sup>adjacent</sup>&frasl;<sub>hypotenuse</sub>" "That is cosine.",
